  "notes": "Percussive stadium alt-pop built on a tom-driven floor. The entry says the identity is \"a four-on-the-floor tom/kick pulse rather than a backbeat-led kit\", so the backbeat class stays straight but the kit is inverted: the kick anchors all four beats at a density of 4, the perc lanes are `tom`, `tomLow`, `tomHigh` and `crash` at the highest perc density and the highest gain offset in this section, and the snare sits under a large gated tail with a low ghost probability. \"Handclaps and stomps in place of hats\" is `hihat.continuous` false at `fillDensity` 0.06, and \"fills are tom cascades, not snare rolls\" is the roll vocabulary switched off with the ladder disabled. No `bass808` block: \"distorted sub and synth bass doubling the tom pulse; low end is deliberately blunt and mono\", which is a kick mirror at 0.97 with a single passing tone and the narrowest bass register here. Harmony is the entry's stated pair, \"i—VI—III—VII or i—VII—VI … with a sustained tonic drone\", so those two families lead and a tonic family carries the drone. Melody encodes \"chant-like with a short repeated cell in verses and a shouted wide-interval hook\" as a two-to-three-pitch motif with a raised `octaveJumpProb`; \"countermelody is a distorted synth or vocal-chop riff\" is `answer_lick` plus `bell_echo`. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research says \"tempo/key bands inferred\": every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the melody register and `bpm.mode` 130 (the midpoint of the stated 120—140 anthem core) are INFERRED, and the entry's [LOW-CONF] mark on the rock-tenor claim is repeated here.",
